  "description": "24\"/26\" Full Suspension bike for kids 7-10.Lightweight, durable and designed for downhill bike park trails and enduro.\nAdjustable geometry USED TO mean throwing 26\" wheels on your kid's bike and jacking the entire bike and the rider's position in the cockpit up by an inch. We set out to change that. Meet the Rokk, a.k.a the G.O.A.T of adjustable geo!\nThe Rokk's uniquely positioned flip-chip shortens/lengthens the rear end of the bike meaning you're not just putting big wheels on a small bike's back end. When you flip the chip, it actually puts the bottom bracket, cranks, and pedals in the right position, even taking into account the clearance needed for different crank lengths appropriate for each wheel size. The riding position stays long, low and slack for both 24\" and 26\" set-up.\nThis machine is shred-ready with solid spec out of the box. It boasts Rock Shox suspension with a trunion mount Deluxe shock with 140mm of finely tuned rear travel and a 140mm Revelation fork with adjustable compression and rebound. A SRAM 11-speed NX drivetrain and an upright climbing position make this bike a true G.O.A.T on the climb while SRAM Level brakes handle all your little ripper can dish out on the descent.\nBrood components make up the balance with 145mm Styx cranks, a 32T direct-mount narrow-wide chainwheel, TR27 tubeless-ready wheelset rolling on tubeless-ready Maxtion tires. Tenderiderz lock-on grips and Throne Pivotal saddle round out the highlights of the build.",
